WEBVTT

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:21.080
<i>I work...</i>

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.290
WHITE BLOOD CELL

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:24.000
<i>and work...</i>

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.840
<i>and work...</i>

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.470
What are you doing?
Deliver that oxygen!

00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.100
I work and work and work...

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:44.480
but it doesn't make any difference!

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:48.520
Just what is it that we're all working for?

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:52.650
You have to keep on working anyway.

00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.450
As long as you have a job to do.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:09.960
Cells at Work!
CODE BLACK

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.920
EPISODE 1:
SMOKING, BACTERIA,
AND THE BEGINNING OF THE END

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:13.920
Welcome, everyone.

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:17.640
Now that you've graduated
from Erythroblast status,

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.180
as of today, you'll be working
with us as Red Blood Cells.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:27.350
We have great expectations of you all
as you work for the bright future of this world!

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.690
Since we all share the same mission,
we are like family.

00:01:32.020 --> 00:01:35.780
Let's help each other out,
join forces and do our best together.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.040
CELL

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.750
<i>This is the body in which
you'll be working, starting today.</i>

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.460
<i>Throughout the film you're about to see,</i>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.630
<i>we'll be introducing you to the various systems
and cells inside this body.</i>

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:03.560
<i>First, the path that you Red Blood Cells will be taking
to deliver oxygen, the blood vessel.</i>

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.720
<i>A route not only for you...</i>

00:02:05.220 --> 00:02:08.690
<i>but also for the White Blood Cells who eliminate
foreign substances that enter the body...</i>

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:13.650
<i>the Killer T Cells who eliminate cells
infected by viruses...</i>

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:17.240
<i>and the Macrophages
who clean up the body.</i>

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.110
<i>As you can see,
it's a pathway for all types of cells.</i>

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:25.160
<i>And these are the Platelets
who work to repair damaged blood vessels.</i>

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.160
PLATELETS

00:02:25.370 --> 00:02:27.540
<i>- Hello!
- Hello!</i>

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.120
<i>They just said hello to us!</i>

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.920
<i>Greetings are essential if you're going
to have a good day at work, right?</i>

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:40.430
<i>And here are the internal organs
which are indispensable for the work you'll be doing.</i>

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:43.100
Each one serves its own crucial role...

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.060
<i>and it's here that you'll find the cells</i>

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.680
<i>who can be considered specialists
in their respective fields at work.</i>

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.650
<i>Among them are organs
that will look after your Red Blood Cells.</i>

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.530
Can't wait for that!

00:02:57.480 --> 00:02:58.440
Yep.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.820
<i>And now, why don't we hear
from one of them?</i>

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:04.280
<i>Gastric Chief Cell will speak to us now.</i>

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.330
<i>What are you doing right now?</i>

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.410
<i>This here's digestion.</i>

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:12.670
<i>It's an important process
for absorbing nutrients.</i>

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.960
<i>Can you say a few words
to our newly-joined Red Blood Cells?</i>

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.630
<i>Let's see.</i>

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:23.760
<i>When you come to the stomach
to make deliveries, tell us your names.</i>

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:26.640
<i>It's a lot more pleasant to work
with a familiar face</i>

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:30.060
<i>than with someone
you don't even know by name.</i>

00:03:30.520 --> 00:03:33.560
<i>We'll be waiting for you guys!</i>

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:39.030
<i>You may work in different systems,
but you're all friends working in the same body.</i>

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.700
<i>By interacting,
you can improve the work environment.</i>

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:49.410
That's it for our introductory video.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:53.670
You will now separate into groups,
and start your on-the-job training.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.670
Any questions?

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:56.000
Yes!

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:56.840
Go on.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:00.590
Uh, can you tell us
how much overtime to expect?

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.970
We can't say that there won't be any,

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:05.260
but we've been working toward
reducing overtime as much as possible.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:07.720
You know, what they call "work-style reforms."

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.680
Seriously? Good to know!

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:15.100
Efficient, shortened workdays
and increased benefits are part of our plan

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.520
to provide you with security
in the workplace.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:24.240
Hey, this job's gonna be easier than I thought!

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.120
Uh, yeah.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:27.950
It seems like a friendly environment,

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:31.000
and the people from the other systems
seemed nice, too.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.080
Hey, what are you looking at?

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.580
I need to learn all our delivery destinations.

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:40.750
How serious are you?
Can't we just figure that out during OJT?

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:42.260
Well, yeah, I guess.

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:47.680
We have one simple job, delivering oxygen,
so there's no need to get so gung-ho about it.

00:04:49.430 --> 00:04:51.140
You're late, rookies.

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.060
Oh, are you the senpais
who'll be training us in the field?

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.100
Grab your oxygen now. Come on.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:59.520
Hurry up! Two boxes per person!

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:00.070
R-Right!

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.950
What are we going to do now?

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.990
Your jobs, what else?
Transport that oxygen.

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.030
We're working already?

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.330
But we heard that we'd be training—

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.790
We don't have time to train you.
Learn on the job.

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:19.840
This body is short on both manpower and time.
Now get going.

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.800
Huh? What about the work-style reforms?

00:05:23.380 --> 00:05:26.510
All you're ever going to find here
is never-ending toil.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.130
Huh?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:29.930
If you're a Red Blood Cell,

00:05:29.930 --> 00:05:33.020
then deliver, deliver,
deliver oxygen until you drop!

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:39.190
<i>The aortic valve will now open.</i>

00:05:40.520 --> 00:05:43.400
<i>Let's make today
another day without injuries...</i>

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.530
<i>and work energetically
with a smile on our faces!</i>

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.660
Go! Go! Go!
Run! Run! Run!

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.120
Run until you drop! Work!

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.580
Keep working until your strength is sapped!

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.540
<i>This is the moment that it started.</i>

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:04.000
<i>The black labor within this body!</i>

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:08.050
This is rough!

00:06:08.970 --> 00:06:10.800
Don't slow down! Hurry up!

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:11.930
Right!

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:15.850
What is this? I never signed up
for anything like this!

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.640
Idiot!

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.400
AC1677! You need to go this way!

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:20.980
Right.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:27.900
Which way is the stomach?

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:31.870
You're in our way! Move it!

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.240
Oh! Sorry!

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:37.120
Platelet, hello—

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.130
Just skip the formalities and get out
of our way! Get a life, will you?

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:43.460
Oh, hey, I'm sorry!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:50.090
Sorry about that.
It's just that we're in a hurry.

00:06:53.970 --> 00:07:01.650
<i>The stomach. Stores all ingested food
and disinfects it with gastric acid secretions.</i>

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:08.190
<i>In addition, a digestive enzyme called "pespin"
breaks down food, turning it into a paste,</i>

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:11.030
<i>thus completing the first stage of digestion.</i>

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:13.870
Sorry to keep you waiting for your oxygen.

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.700
Oh, you were in that training video.

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.910
You're too damn slow!

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:23.250
How long does it take
to deliver one canister of oxygen?

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:26.340
I'm sorry.
I only just started working today—

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:31.050
What do I care? Once you're in the field,
it doesn't matter if you're a rookie or a veteran!

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:32.220
Right! Sorry!

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:38.470
Oh, and also... this is my first day,
and I'm AA2153.

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:39.560
Huh?

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.100
Th-That's my name.

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:43.100
Who the cell has time to remember names?

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.570
Every one of you has
the same damn face and name!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:47.610
Read the room, will you?

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:51.990
But in that video, you said
you wanted to know our names.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:56.200
Huh? They're still using that thing?
From ages ago?

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:57.240
What?

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:03.210
Since we recorded that video, this body's gone
so downhill, you can't even compare it to before!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.290
I don't have a second to spare like I did then.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.170
How did that happen?

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.260
Not just fatigue, but sleep deprivation to boot.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:15.640
Not to mention excessive eating and drinking.

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.270
No matter how hard we work,
it's only getting worse and worse.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:21.100
But...

00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:23.600
Now you know, so next time,
bring that oxygen faster!

00:08:23.600 --> 00:08:25.310
R-Right!

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:38.990
Hey, Red Blood Cell!

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.950
You've really been skimping
on the oxygen supply lately!

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:48.090
I'm sorry. We've been ordered to prioritize
deliveries to the main organs, so...

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:51.670
Huh? So, the cells in the extremities
can just die, is that it?

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:53.920
P-Please forgive me.

00:08:55.630 --> 00:08:57.140
Really sorry about this.

00:08:58.010 --> 00:09:01.310
We'll be able to provide you
with a massive supply of fresh oxygen soon,

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:02.770
and you'll be first on our list.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.100
Really?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.600
This is just a special deal for you, ma'am.

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:10.730
Now, then, we'll be off.
Let's go, rookie.

00:09:14.150 --> 00:09:16.070
Thank you very much, Senpai.

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.530
So, there's going to be
a massive supply of fresh oxygen?

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:21.490
No, I made that up.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.490
Huh?

00:09:22.490 --> 00:09:25.080
Well, we'd never get anything done
if we actually listened to all the complaints.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.790
Oh, so that's it?

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.290
Oh, I'm sorry to make you carry the oxygen!

00:09:32.050 --> 00:09:35.010
Hold it diagonally, like this,
and it'll be more stable.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:37.130
Hey, you're right!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:40.970
You were out of luck,
starting here at a time like this.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:45.480
Normally, it's part of our job to show
the ropes to the rookies...

00:09:45.730 --> 00:09:48.900
but there isn't a single person here
who has that kind of time.

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.900
Why are we so short-handed?

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:53.980
It's probably due to stress.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:58.240
To prioritize the vitals,
there's been less bloodflow to the extremities.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:02.740
Years ago, this body was nothing like this.

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:08.710
Let's go! The higher-ups will give us an earful
if we don't fulfill our quotas, right?

00:10:09.210 --> 00:10:10.330
Senpai!

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:15.010
Senpai, how can you possibly smile
when things are like this?

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:16.840
Hey, it's simple!

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:19.090
All you have to do
is suppress your emotions.

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:19.800
Huh?

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:23.680
"I want to rest."
"I want to have an easy time."

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.640
Hoping for that kind of thing
is what brings you anguish.

00:10:26.980 --> 00:10:31.020
If you suppress all of your emotions,
you can keep smiling.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.990
True. His eyes aren't smiling.

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:42.660
What's going on here?
The vessel's all bumpy!

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:45.370
Watch your step, rookie.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.660
Okay.

00:10:49.580 --> 00:10:50.580
Hey, dummy!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:53.500
Don't ever let go of that oxygen!
It's more precious than life itself!

00:10:55.130 --> 00:10:56.880
Is that the LDL guys?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.170
Hey, come back here!

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:01.050
Get a hold of yourself. Can you stand?

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:01.840
Yes.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.180
Who were they?

00:11:03.510 --> 00:11:06.810
LDL. The bad cholesterol guys.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:11.020
That was them illegally disposing
of cholesterol secreted by the liver.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:12.270
Illegal disposal?

00:11:12.810 --> 00:11:17.400
Seriously, if this ends up blocking the vessel
and causing arterial sclerosis,

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:19.530
we won't be able to get through.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.410
Won't be able to get through?

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:23.160
Because of oxidation in the body.

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:24.530
Oxidation...

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:26.740
This is also due to stress.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:34.750
Stress generates increased levels of active oxygen,
creating bumps on the vessel walls.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:37.000
That's why it's so bumpy.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:42.380
And now that resistance is also low,
I hear that more germs have shown up.

00:11:42.380 --> 00:11:43.800
Germs...

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:46.430
Um...

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:48.890
This body...

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:52.100
Is it going to be all right?

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:55.900
Don't worry about stuff like that!

00:11:56.230 --> 00:12:00.820
All we need to do is suppress our emotions
and deliver oxygen in silence!

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:10.750
We're back.
So, I've gone around once.

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.210
You can take a break
before starting the second round.

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:15.130
Okay.

00:12:15.380 --> 00:12:17.000
I'm going to take a look over there.

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.090
I'm exhausted.

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:22.880
- Get up.
- Huh?

00:12:22.880 --> 00:12:24.970
Who said you could take a break?

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.930
We don't have time for breaks!

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:29.890
Huh? Um...

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:32.270
Hey, come on.

00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:37.230
He just went around the whole body on his first job.
Of course, that's got to tire him out some...

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:39.400
It's too soon to whine and give up.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:43.490
We've got to make so many trips
around the body a day.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.410
When we were rookies, we took it easier—

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:49.080
And we're paying for that now, aren't we?

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:53.660
If you have time to reminisce
about the old days, get moving.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.210
I can go.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:04.130
Don't coddle the rookies anymore.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.390
If I'm not mistaken,
the road splits off up ahead

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:15.900
into the carotid artery leading to the head,
and the descending aorta leading to the torso.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:17.940
Good job, rookie!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:21.400
This time, we're going to pass through
the digestive system from the descending aorta

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:22.820
to get back to the heart.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:23.490
Okay!

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:29.530
Wh-What's that gas?

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:43.010
- Are you all right?
- Idiot!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:46.090
Don't go near him!
This is carbon monoxide!

00:13:46.510 --> 00:13:48.050
Carbon monoxide?

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:52.520
Us Red Blood Cells contain
tons of hemoglobin.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.770
Hemoglobin has a binding affinity
with carbon monoxide!

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:01.730
<i>Hemoglobin. The protein containing
the red pigment that gives blood its red color.</i>

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:08.200
<i>By binding with oxygen, it enables Red Blood Cells
to transport oxygen throughout the body.</i>

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:12.280
If we bind with carbon monoxide,
we won't be able to deliver oxygen!

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:13.240
Huh?

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:16.750
Meaning that the body will become
oxygen-deprived!

00:14:17.330 --> 00:14:19.710
Carbon monoxide detected
within the blood vessel!

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:21.340
Irritation to the central nervous system!

00:14:21.340 --> 00:14:23.300
It seems like some kind of toxin
has been introduced.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:25.010
A toxin?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.880
The heart rate's going up!
Blood pressure rising!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.720
The capillaries are constricting!

00:14:30.180 --> 00:14:32.640
Wh-What's going on? The walls are...

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.810
Have you analyzed the toxin?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.270
The acetylcholine receptors
are in a state of agitation,

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.520
and the chain of command
has been disrupted!

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:46.150
<i>Acetylcholine receptors.</i>

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:50.110
<i>They exist in the synapses
and are made of protein.</i>

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:53.830
<i>They receive the neurotransmitter
acetylcholine...</i>

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.790
<i>sending signals across the nerve network,</i>

00:14:56.790 --> 00:15:00.750
<i>and controlling the smooth muscles,
skeletal muscles and sweat glands.</i>

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:05.210
The acetylcohline receptors
have been affected? Don't tell me it's...

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:08.920
E-Everybody?

00:15:09.430 --> 00:15:11.260
W-We have to save them!

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:15.310
It's too late!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:17.850
These guys have turned
into carboxyhemoglobin!

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.060
<i>Carboxyhemoglobin.</i>

00:15:21.060 --> 00:15:24.270
<i>Formed when hemoglobin binds
with carbon monoxide.</i>

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:28.820
<i>Red Blood Cells are unable
to deliver oxygen in this state.</i>

00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.660
But where did this carbon monoxide come from?

00:15:33.030 --> 00:15:33.950
Senpai!

00:15:34.990 --> 00:15:36.040
Look.

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.120
Huh?

00:15:39.460 --> 00:15:43.290
Bacteria's reached the blood vessel...
at a time like this?

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:44.880
Bacteria?

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.090
Those are Pneumococci!

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:54.680
<i>Pneumococci. Pathogenic bacteria that trigger
pneumonia, septicemia and the like.</i>

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.560
<i>A highly durable and toxic bacteria.</i>

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.440
What should we do?

00:16:07.900 --> 00:16:09.110
Nothing we can do but run.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:12.360
They attack cells, seeking nutrients!

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:15.120
We're going to end up
getting ruptured, too!

00:16:26.340 --> 00:16:27.250
That's...

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:34.220
A cleaner cell who eliminates
germs from the body...

00:16:35.680 --> 00:16:37.050
White Blood Cell!

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:42.980
<i>White Blood Cell or Neutrophil.</i>

00:16:43.310 --> 00:16:45.310
<i>Its main job is to eliminate foreign substances</i>

00:16:45.310 --> 00:16:49.650
<i>such as bacteria and viruses
that have invaded the body from the outside.</i>

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:51.940
Sorry I got here late.

00:16:52.150 --> 00:16:56.120
The germs have been proliferating all over the place,
so we've been really swamped.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:00.950
Are you a rookie?

00:17:01.750 --> 00:17:03.960
Y-Yes.

00:17:05.080 --> 00:17:06.790
Let me take care of this.

00:17:19.310 --> 00:17:20.720
Let's go, rookie.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:22.310
Huh? Go where?

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.060
Where do you think?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:27.020
We're going to deliver this oxygen.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.570
If the delivery of oxygen is halted,
the cells will die of necrosis.

00:17:32.030 --> 00:17:33.990
Our job doesn't allow for breaks.

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:36.110
B-But...

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:40.330
In a situation like this,
even if we're under orders...

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:44.580
You must be kidding me!
I can't take this job anymore!

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:48.710
Don't ever forget this, rookie.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.800
The moment us Red Blood Cells mature,

00:17:53.130 --> 00:17:56.930
we discard everything that normal cells have.

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:59.890
Our cell nuclei, our mitochondria,
all of our organelles.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:05.680
And we become cells that are 90% hemoglobin,
cells that are dedicated to delivering oxygen.

00:18:06.480 --> 00:18:09.480
We spend our entire lives
delivering oxygen to the entire body,

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:13.940
traveling the same route
over and over 200,000... 300,000 times!

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:16.360
This isn't an order.

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.370
There's nothing else that we can do!

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:26.580
Don't think about anything,
suppress your emotions and transport the oxygen!

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:28.710
We don't need any wimps here.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:34.000
You retrieve the oxygen and take
the descending aorta to head back to the lungs.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:34.760
Huh?

00:18:34.760 --> 00:18:36.510
That route is still safe.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:40.470
I'll take the carotid artery
to transport your oxygen to the brain.

00:18:41.260 --> 00:18:43.430
Because the brain cells are our top priority.

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:45.930
The carotid artery?

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:50.020
White Blood Cell Lady!

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:51.810
We're counting on you!

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:55.280
Senpai, it's no good! If you do that—

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:56.900
I'm leaving the rest to you.

00:18:57.440 --> 00:18:59.610
Make sure you become a fine Red Blood Cell.

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:04.030
Sorry I couldn't pass the baton to you
in a better environment.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:05.790
Senpai!

00:19:25.850 --> 00:19:27.220
Emotions...

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:29.980
No way is it easy to suppress them.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.940
Not for any cell...

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:38.990
Senpai!

00:19:40.950 --> 00:19:43.410
Don't let his resolve have been for nothing.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.410
Come with me.

00:19:48.160 --> 00:19:50.790
<i>The carbon monoxide advisory
has been lifted.</i>

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:54.340
<i>All cells, please be careful
when you head outside!</i>

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.590
Have you calmed down a little?

00:19:56.590 --> 00:20:01.470
Yes. Thank you for saving me,
White Blood Cell.

00:20:01.840 --> 00:20:04.300
I just did my job, that's all.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.850
Um, White Blood Cell?

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:13.730
Are our jobs really worth
risking our lives for?

00:20:17.610 --> 00:20:21.900
We might be working
so that we can find the answer to that.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:23.660
Where are you going?

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:28.540
To the lungs. I'm going to see
what caused the carbon monoxide outbreak.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:32.460
<i>Lungs.</i>

00:20:32.670 --> 00:20:35.960
<i>The organs that absorb oxygen
from the air into the body...</i>

00:20:36.460 --> 00:20:43.430
<i>and expel the carbon dioxide delivered
by the Red Blood Cells back into the air.</i>

00:20:44.300 --> 00:20:46.390
How did it get so dirty?

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:51.350
Today's emergency was caused by smoking.
For the first time in ten years, that is.

00:20:51.600 --> 00:20:54.310
Smoking?
And this has happened before?

00:20:54.690 --> 00:20:58.230
Look up there.
That's the grime from before.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:21:01.030
Just when it was finally starting to get clean...

00:21:01.490 --> 00:21:02.950
I hear that they detected nicotine,

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:07.740
a toxin that affects the acetylcholine
receptors in the nerve tract.

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:12.580
Why would this body deliberately
ingest something like that?

00:21:12.830 --> 00:21:15.960
Because one of its effects
is temporary pleasure.

00:21:16.420 --> 00:21:19.550
Not only that,
but nicotine is also addictive.

00:21:20.210 --> 00:21:22.880
The same thing is going to happen
again and again.

00:21:23.130 --> 00:21:24.840
You should keep that in mind.

00:21:24.840 --> 00:21:27.390
B-But...

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:34.020
<i>Red Blood Cells, receive your oxygen at once
and deliver it to the entire body!</i>

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:39.480
<i>Repeat, receive your oxygen at once
and deliver it to the entire body!</i>

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:42.230
<i>The resumption of smoking
after ten years...</i>

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:47.870
<i>That was only the beginning
of the dangers awaiting this body.</i>

00:23:19.460 --> 00:23:21.460
PREVIEW

00:23:20.370 --> 00:23:21.460
No way!

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:24.630
I've always wanted to visit the liver!

00:23:22.840 --> 00:23:24.630
LIVER

00:23:24.630 --> 00:23:26.090
Calm down.

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.170
This is alcohol.

00:23:26.340 --> 00:23:27.300
ALCOHOL

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:29.510
PRIDE

00:23:28.170 --> 00:23:32.930
As long as they're here,
I don't want them to see my weak side.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.970
THE LIVER, ALCOHOL, AND PRIDE
